From: Shipwright
Subject: [PATCH] Qt 6 input context for Keel apps on Lipstick

Two faults in the Qt 6 input context (Chum's qt6-sfos-maliit-
platforminputcontext), found on the Jolla Phone:

- containerConnectionInterface was only assigned when
  FLATPAK_MALIIT_CONTAINER_DBUS is set and was left uninitialised
  otherwise, so the first updateInputMethodArea from maliit-server
  dereferenced garbage: every Qt 6 app crashed when its keyboard opened.
- keyboardRect() returned an empty rectangle ("taken care by
  compositor"). Keel apps run on Lipstick directly and lay out around
  QInputMethod::keyboardRectangle, as Silica does on Qt 5, so text
  fields stayed under the keyboard.

SPDX-FileCopyrightText: 2026 Patrick Quinn
SPDX-License-Identifier: LGPL-2.1-only
---
diff --git a/input-context/minputcontext.cpp b/input-context/minputcontext.cpp
index 97240fc..3130688 100644
--- a/input-context/minputcontext.cpp
+++ b/input-context/minputcontext.cpp
@@ -61,6 +61,7 @@ bool MInputContext::debug = false;
 
 MInputContext::MInputContext()
     : imServer(0),
+      containerConnectionInterface(nullptr),
       active(false),
       inputPanelState(InputPanelHidden),
       preeditCursorPos(-1),
@@ -413,8 +414,10 @@ bool MInputContext::filterEvent(const QEvent *event)
 
 QRectF MInputContext::keyboardRect() const
 {
-    return QRectF();
-    //return keyboardRectangle;
+    // Shipwright: Qt 6 apps on Lipstick itself (Keel) lay out around the
+    // keyboard from QInputMethod::keyboardRectangle, as Silica on Qt 5 does;
+    // an empty rectangle left text fields under the keyboard.
+    return keyboardRectangle;
 }
 
 bool MInputContext::isAnimating() const
